WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Good morning, Hank, it's January 10th 2012, the day that The Fault In Our Stars comes out!

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:05.910
It's actually Monday January 9th

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.687
but I have to make this video now because tomorrow I got to be doing a bunch of things.

00:00:08.687 --> 00:00:11.580
It's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions from real nerdfighters.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:12.240
"How you doing?"

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.540
Good, I'm just a tiny bit stressed out. I have to leave my family for a month,

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:17.399
which is kind of a bummer, but I'm excited to go on tour. How are YOU doing?

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.199
You can't answer, you're inside of the camera.

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:21.760
"I hope I get my copy today so I can lick your signature."

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.249
Um that's not a question, but I don't recommend licking sharpie that- that's bad for you.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.560
"So what inspired you to write The Fault In Our Stars? "

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.140
Almost twelve years ago, I worked as a student Chaplain at a children's hospital,

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.320
ever since then I've been trying to write a funny, honest story about it and

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.840
It just, y'know, took a while.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:36.760
Long while.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.669
"Do you think The Fault In Our Stars is your best book yet?"

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.520
I don't know. The reviews have definitely been better than for any of my other books,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.649
but authors shouldn't be trusted to judge their own work;

00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:48.200
I don't think like Mark Twain thought that his best book was Joan Of Arc. Yeah. No.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.900
Hank, I gotta go pack and stuff. Walk with me.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.420
"Could an unladen swallow carry a copy of The Fault In Our Stars in its talons?"

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.820
Well definitionally not, as it would then be a laden swallow.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.040
Do you like this tie?

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.000
"Was it hard to write The Fault In Our Stars as a parent?"

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.600
I don't think I could write it UNTIL I was a parent.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.500
"How much research did you have to do about the medical stuff in the The Fault In Our Stars?"

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.460
More than a hypochondriac probably should.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.660
"What made you decide to write this one from a girl's point of view?"

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:09.809
That's pretty hard to answer without spoilers.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.040
But part of it was that I wanted to think about the way gender constructions

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.670
shape our understanding of what constitutes heroism.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.980
"Do you think V for Vendetta is a proponent of democracy or anarchy?"

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:22.400
I think V for Vendetta is primarily a proponent of a very specific and pervasive idea of heroism.

00:01:22.401 --> 00:01:23.909
"Will you do peanut butter face?"

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:27.000
I'm in an airport, people'll think that I'm crazy .Alright, fine, hold on.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.540
Do you guys have any peanut butter crackers?

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:29.700
These are the best I could do.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:30.880
Happy?

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:34.560
"Will I feel out of the loop if I haven't read Looking For Alaska?"

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.700
No, it's not like Harry Potter;

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.240
my books don't have anything to do with each other.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.380
"What genre of music are The Hectic Glow?"

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:40.589
The genre of awesome.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.280
"Hey, my pre-order wasn't signed."

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:42.940
Don't panic.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:47.200
Just email &lt;sparksflyup@gmail.com&gt; with your name, address and the place where you ordered the book.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.860
"Did you ever get emotional while writing this book?"

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:49.680
Yeah, quite a bit actually

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:50.560
but I'm a crier.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.040
"Wait is The Fault In Our Stars gonna make me cry or laugh or what?"

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.020
Well, ideally it's going to make you feel

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.640
ALL OF THE THINGS.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.700
[Singing] People in the airport think that I'm crazy, the people in the airport think that I'm crazy.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.200
I probably shouldn't have done that while doing a dance. That's probably-

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.280
Let's face it. There's nobody in the airport.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.100
Seriously, I got this whole section to myself.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.269
There were some people here

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.980
but they left when I started talking into a video camera.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.720
"Was Esther an inspiration for this book?"

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:16.520
Definitely. There's no way I could have ever written The Fault In Our Stars unless I'd known Esther.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:21.560
But at the same time it's really important to note that Hazel is not Esther. The book is made up.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.480
I wrote a novel. I promise.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.800
"Does The Fault In Our Stars contain anything about fruit?"

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.980
I don't think so.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.480
I think- that might be one of its insufficiencies is a failure...

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.680
to tackle fruit.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.960
"Are there any tickets left to anywhere on the Tour De Nerdfighting?"

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.060
Yeah, if you live near New Orleans, Houston, Austin Phoenix, Albuquerque, Seattle or San Francisco.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.760
Otherwise no, I'm sorry.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.200
Ticket info in the doobly-doo.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.660
Is this real life?!

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.660
HEEEEEY

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.600
"Has Nerdfighteria influenced your writing at all?"

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.680
As you'll probably see in reading it,

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.500
Nerdfighteria has shaped this book in so many ways that I can't even list them .

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.780
"What was your favorite moment in the creation of The Fault In Our Stars?"

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.880
So, Hank, Islamic mystics have this word "Fanaa"

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.660
which means like dissolution or annihilation of the self

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:04.120
and for me, that's what reading and writing do, when they're working

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.220
and when I was writing The Fault In Our Stars,

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:10.560
I was very, very lucky to have many moments where I felt like I wasn't me,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.720
like I was somehow

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.780
transcending the limits of myself

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.200
and that was really great.

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:17.920
And I can only hope that readers will have that experience.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.189
Thank you all for reading The Fault In Our Stars,

00:03:20.189 --> 00:03:21.640
I hope that you like it.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.260
DFTBA, best wishes.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.240
Hank, I will see you in a minute when I go over to your room.

